# A great run on Fisherman's Wharf (the score tiers' measure): Jefferson's north curb coming from Pier 39 every
# 10 s (the teleport stands in for rolling back; the promenade's granite edges north of Pier 7 that this run
# used are not in the squeezed city): a boneless onto it, a nosegrind along it for 24 m (as long as the
# promenade's edge) and a 360 flip off: 6,330; twelve, 75,960. Pro (16,500) on the third, Sick (52,000) on the
# ninth: Sick is set from how often a decent player reaches it (about a third, ./skate feel --tour), not as 91%
# of this run (69,000, which a decent player never reached in 50). (On the promenade edge it was 9,452,
# PROMENADE EDGE on the pop; twelve, 113,424, Sick 103,000.)
